WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:05.520
The reason we're replacing the

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.830
roundabout with traffic signals is that

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:10.139
over the last 10 years the traffic

00:00:10.139 --> 00:00:12.059
volumes  have increased from seventeen

00:00:12.059 --> 00:00:14.730
thousand vehicles a day to 24,000 vehicles

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:17.130
a day and so the roundabout just isn't

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:19.080
coping with that level of traffic

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.180
especially at peak times.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:24.140
So traffic signals provide a much better and more

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.430
efficient way of managing that traffic

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:28.189
and an added advantage of the traffic

00:00:28.199 --> 00:00:30.029
signals is for pedestrians.

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:32.489
Especially with schools in the area

00:00:32.489 --> 00:00:34.680
that will provide a much safer route for

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:36.600
children to cross and get to the schools.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:42.000
So the first stage of the work is working on

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.500
the eastern side of the road and that's

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.660
where the widening is taking place but

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:47.969
also more importantly it'll enable a new

00:00:47.969 --> 00:00:50.219
footpath to be constructed during the

00:00:50.219 --> 00:00:51.930
school holidays and by the time the

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:54.329
schools start again there will be a new

00:00:54.329 --> 00:00:56.030
footpath constructed, so that will

00:00:56.039 --> 00:00:59.010
provide much a safer environment for the

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:01.469
school children while the construction

00:01:01.469 --> 00:01:03.289
work then continues after that.

00:01:05.159 --> 00:01:06.780
With a project of this size and

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:08.999
complexity, there will be an impact on

00:01:08.999 --> 00:01:11.779
commuters and general traffic.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:14.939
Just be patient if you're using the intersection

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.920
but consider using an alternative route if  you can

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:20.360
and certainly avoid peak times if you can.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:23.040
When the work's finished, the intersection finished

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.460
it's going to be a much better intersection and traffic will

00:01:25.469 --> 00:01:27.289
be flowing much more freely

00:01:27.289 --> 00:01:30.719
so we think the benefits of the end result will be

00:01:30.719 --> 00:01:33.599
fantastic and it's just a case of being

00:01:33.599 --> 00:01:35.189
patient while we carry out the

00:01:35.189 --> 00:01:36.369
construction work.

